P4b. the closure of d one-demand generators under union

==================================================================
d = 4 generators: speed, residency, accuracy, familiarity
  ordered pairs of generators                : 16
  pairs whose union is NOT itself a generator: 12
  closure under union                        : 15 elements
  2^d - 1                                    : 15
  identical                                  : True
  ordered pairs unresolvable INSIDE the closure: 0 of 225
  names a design must write down             : 4 (the generators)
  elements a consumer can name anyway        : 15 (formal joins of them)

==================================================================
d = 3 generators: speed, residency, accuracy
  ordered pairs of generators                : 9
  pairs whose union is NOT itself a generator: 6
  closure under union                        : 7 elements
  2^d - 1                                    : 7
  identical                                  : True
  ordered pairs unresolvable INSIDE the closure: 0 of 49
  names a design must write down             : 3 (the generators)
  elements a consumer can name anyway        : 7 (formal joins of them)

==================================================================
d = 5 generators: speed, residency, accuracy, familiarity, reproducibility
  ordered pairs of generators                : 25
  pairs whose union is NOT itself a generator: 20
  closure under union                        : 31 elements
  2^d - 1                                    : 31
  identical                                  : True
  ordered pairs unresolvable INSIDE the closure: 0 of 961
  names a design must write down             : 5 (the generators)
  elements a consumer can name anyway        : 31 (formal joins of them)

==================================================================
growth: adding one generator doubles the carrier and adds ONE name.
  d = 2  carrier =    3  names = 2
  d = 3  carrier =    7  names = 3
  d = 4  carrier =   15  names = 4
  d = 5  carrier =   31  names = 5
  d = 6  carrier =   63  names = 6
  d = 7  carrier =  127  names = 7
  d = 8  carrier =  255  names = 8

So `93` section 4's stated cost of response (a), that every question about
a strategy must be answered per coordinate rather than looked up per
marker, is the cost of the structure being GENERATED. That is the same cost
a formal union type carries in a type system with unions, and it is what
buys totality: zero unresolvable pairs against 12 of 16 on the flat set.

Note what this does NOT settle. It says the join is total and lawful on the
demand side. It says nothing about whether the demand side is where the
resolution question lives, which P3 attacks separately.
